        <mxCell id="note_how" value="&lt;b&gt;How it holds together&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;OpenBao never starts sealed for long: each pod unwraps its root key from floci (the local stand-in for a cloud KMS), so the bootstrap Job only initialises it once, writes the recovery key, seeds KV, creates the eso-reader / db-configurator / oidc-configurator roles and revokes the root token. External Secrets logs in with Kubernetes auth and re-reads every hour; notification's password comes from the database engine instead and is re-read every minute, because OpenBao rotates it. Since OpenBao 2.7 the awskms seal is an external KMS plugin, downloaded once and cached on the Raft PVC. Every request and response is written as one audit JSON line on stdout (active node only, secret values HMAC-ed), which Vector ships to VictoriaLogs and ClickHouse; vmagent scrapes /v1/sys/metrics." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1190" width="1355" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_planned" value="&lt;b&gt;Planned, not deployed&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;TLS on the OpenBao listener, a real cloud KMS instead of floci, AppRole for CI/CD, per-request dynamic database credentials and internal TLS on homelab-ca (RFC-0020). Locally the edge certificate is issued by homelab-ca; Let's Encrypt DNS-01 with the Cloudflare token is the production path." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1272" width="1355" height="60" as="geometry" />
